#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/termsOfServiceContent.ts:30
msgid "termsOfService.agreementBodyEnd"
msgstr " By creating an account or using Eciperay, you agree to these Terms of Service (\"Terms\"). If you do not agree, do not use the service."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:68
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoAccountBody"
msgstr " email address and display name when you create an account."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:442
msgid "privacyPolicy.tpAnthropicBody"
msgstr " for AI-assisted recipe features."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:427
msgid "privacyPolicy.tpSupabaseBody"
msgstr " for authentication, database storage, and image file storage."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:453
msgid "privacyPolicy.tpOpenaiBody"
msgstr " for certain image-related AI features."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:464
msgid "privacyPolicy.tpPosthogBody"
msgstr " for product analytics, session replay, error tracking, application logging, and feature-flag or experiment tooling. PostHog processes usage and diagnostic data on our behalf to help us understand how Eciperay is used and to fix problems. When you are signed in, analytics data may be linked to your account identifier and email address. PostHog does not receive your recipe content or AI chat messages unless that information appears on screen during a session replay."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:260
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoFeedbackBody"
msgstr " if you enable the feedback shortcut in Profile settings and submit feedback, we collect the message you write, whether you marked it as a bug, the page or screen you were on, and related diagnostic context (including a session identifier and, when available, a link to a session replay). Feedback is sent to PostHog on our behalf. Do not include passwords, tokens, or other sensitive personal information in feedback messages."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:185
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoAiBody"
msgstr " messages you send in AI-assisted recipe features and related draft data."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:275
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoInstallPromptBody"
msgstr " on mobile web browsers, we may show a dismissible banner suggesting the native Eciperay app. If you dismiss it, we store that preference in your browser's local storage for about seven days. That preference is not sent to our servers. Links in the banner go to the Apple App Store or Google Play Store, where their privacy policies apply."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:290
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoReplaysBody"
msgstr " on the web and mobile apps, we may record how you interact with the interface (such as taps, clicks, and navigation). Submitting voluntary feedback starts or ensures a session replay for that session, in addition to replays captured under our normal analytics settings. Text you type into form fields is masked where technically possible, but other on-screen content you view may appear in a replay."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:590
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesAnalyticsBodyStart"
msgstr " on the web you can accept or decline product analytics cookies when prompted. You can clear your browser storage to see the prompt again. To request deletion of analytics data already collected, contact us at "

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:215
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoAnalyticsBody"
msgstr " on the web, we ask for your consent before enabling product analytics cookies and tools such as PostHog. If you accept, we may associate usage and diagnostic data with your account using your user ID and email address when you are signed in. If you decline, we do not load those analytics tools in your browser session. We also collect error reports, crash information, and structured application logs to keep the service reliable."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:170
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoImagesBody"
msgstr " photos you upload for recipes, stored in our file storage service."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:83
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoRecipeContentBody"
msgstr " recipes you create or import, including titles, descriptions, ingredients, instructions, notes, tags, ratings, and source URLs."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:200
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoUsageBody"
msgstr " technical information about how you use Eciperay, such as pages or screens viewed, actions you take (for example creating, importing, or deleting recipes), device and browser type, app version, approximate location derived from IP address, timestamps, and server request logs."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:575
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesFeedbackBody"
msgstr " the feedback shortcut is off by default. You can enable or disable it anytime in Profile settings. On the web, submitting feedback also requires that you have accepted product analytics cookies; if you decline analytics, the shortcut is not available even if enabled. Feedback you submit is processed by PostHog as described above; contact us at the email in Contact us to request deletion of feedback already collected."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:637
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesCameraBody"
msgstr " the mobile app requests camera and photo library access only when you choose to add recipe images. You can deny or revoke these permissions in your device settings."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:35
msgid "privacyPolicy.introductionBody"
msgstr " This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect through the Eciperay recipe management service on the web and mobile apps, how we use it, and the choices you have."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:529
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesSharingBodyEnd"
msgstr " to public recipe pages."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:543
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesAccountBody"
msgstr " update your display name and manage your session from the profile page. You can also download a JSON copy of your profile, recipes, share grants, community ratings, and comments from the profile page."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:113
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoSharedAccessBody"
msgstr " when you are signed in and open a valid share link, we record a grant associating your account with that recipe so it can appear in your Shared with me list. These grants are kept until your account is deleted. Recipe owners do not receive viewer identities in the current version of the service."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:98
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoSharingBody"
msgstr " when you choose to share a recipe via an unlisted link or make it public, anyone with the link (or anyone browsing public recipes) can view that recipe content without signing in. Public recipes also appear in Eciperay's public browse and search results with your display name, title, description, image, status badge, and related metadata. Recipes still marked as ideas are hidden from public browse even if visibility is public. You can change visibility or rotate unlisted links at any time. Anonymous viewers may access shared recipes through our public recipe API; those requests are logged like other server traffic (see usage and diagnostic data below) but are not linked to a viewer account."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:158
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoCommentsBody"
msgstr " when you comment on a recipe you can access, we store your comment text, account, display name, and the recipe revision at the time you posted. Comments are visible to others who can read the recipe. Recipe owners can delete comments on their recipes. Do not include sensitive personal information in comments."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:143
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoRatingsBody"
msgstr " when you rate someone else's shared or public recipe, we store your star rating with your account and the recipe revision you rated. Community averages are shown on accessible recipes and may appear in search previews. Your personal owner rating on recipes you created is stored separately and is not included in community averages."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:230
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoCookieBody"
msgstr " when you respond to our analytics consent banner on the web, we store your choice in your browser's local storage so we can remember it on future visits. You can accept, decline, or withdraw that choice at any time on the privacy choices page linked from every page's footer (\"Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\"); withdrawing removes the stored choice and turns analytics off until you choose again. This preference is not sent to our servers."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:128
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoClonesBody"
msgstr " when you save a copy of someone else's shared recipe, we store a private duplicate in your account and record which recipe it was copied from. The original author is not notified in the current version of the service."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:245
msgid "privacyPolicy.infoFeedbackShortcutBody"
msgstr " when you turn the feedback shortcut on or off in Profile settings, we store that choice in your browser's local storage (web) or on-device storage (mobile apps). This preference is not sent to our servers."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:622
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesCommentsBody"
msgstr " you can edit or delete comments you posted. Recipe owners can delete any comment on their recipes. Comments remain stored until deleted by you, the recipe owner, or when your account is removed."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:558
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesDeletionBodyStart"
msgstr " you can permanently delete your account and associated application data from the profile page. This removes your recipes (including public recipes), comments, ratings, and share grants. If deletion of your authentication account fails after your application data is removed, contact us at "

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:607
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesRatingsBody"
msgstr " you can update or remove your star rating on recipes you can access. Owner personal ratings and community ratings are managed separately as described above."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/legal/privacyPolicyContent.ts:521
msgid "privacyPolicy.choicesSharingBodyStart"
msgstr " you control whether each recipe stays private, is shared via an unlisted link, or is published for public discovery. Unlisted links can be rotated to revoke prior links. When you share a recipe, recipients receive a link that exposes the full recipe content to anyone they forward it to, so review visibility before sharing. Opening a share link while signed in adds the recipe to your Shared with me list until you delete your account. Public recipes may be indexed by search engines and appear in link previews on social platforms; we do not apply "

